<title>FRANCE: All French capital markets in euros Jan 99 - report.</title>
<headline>All French capital markets in euros Jan 99 - report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France and a group of industry professionals said in a report published on Monday all French capital markets, including the stock market, would be converted to a single European currency on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>The report adopts the conclusions of a working group set up by the central bank and the Association Francaise des Etablissements de Credit et des Entreprises d'Investissement (AFECEI), headed by Bank of France deputy governor Herve Hannoun.</p>
<p>The report said French foreign exchange markets, bond and money markets, futures markets and stock markets would all be converted into euros at the launch of a single currency.</p>
</text>
